 <p><span class="mp" data-m="share">📁 File ▾ › Boards and appropriations › ⬇ Export one appropriation…</span> makes a working board file holding one appropriation: its plan, its locked cycles, its execution data and its BAE rows, with the destination list, cost estimates and reprogramming log. It opens on that appropriation, and edits and saves like any board — hand it to an appropriation lead.</p>
-<p><span class="mp" data-m="share">📁 File ▾ › Boards and appropriations › ⬅ Import one appropriation…</span> takes appropriations back from any board file. It lists what the file holds and takes only what you name; each one is checked for work this board did meanwhile and previewed before it replaces anything, and its locked cycles come with it. Nothing else on the board changes.</p>
+<p><span class="mp" data-m="share">📁 File ▾ › Boards and appropriations › ⬅ Import one appropriation…</span> takes appropriations back from any board file. It lists what the file holds and takes only what you name; each one is checked for work this board did meanwhile and previewed before it replaces anything, and its locked cycles come with it. Nothing else on the board changes. A file that carries a locked cycle whose RCN / EEIC list breaks the rule for one — a key repeated, missing, not text or beginning with two underscores, or something in it that is not an entry — is refused, whichever board saved it: a locked cycle’s list stays as it was locked. Such a file opens as a board, and <span class="mp" data-m="share">📁 File ▾ › Boards and appropriations › ⬅ Import a full board (new version)…</span> takes it whole.</p>
 <p><span class="mp" data-m="share">📁 File ▾ › Boards and appropriations › ⇊ Import several boards at once…</span> merges several board files in one go. It takes all of them or none: every file is read and checked first — which appropriation it is, that no two are for the same one, its services against that appropriation’s (a different order is matched up by name if you say so) — and if any is refused, cannot be read, or you answer No, nothing is imported and it says why. It is off while a locked cycle is on screen. Should the board on screen still refuse its appropriation once the files are written, every list is put back and read back; if one cannot be put back, it says which lists hold what, holds 💾 Save and the shared folder, and offers this board as it was and each file it took — save them before anything else, as after a full import that stopped part-way. <span class="mp" data-m="share">📁 File ▾ › Boards and appropriations › 🔁 Appropriation packages…</span> hands an appropriation to its manager and takes it back against a ledger.</p>
 </section>
